**Definition 1.3 (Raw two-world $M$ equations).** For each label $i=1,2$
use coordinates $t_i,b_i,e_i,q_{i0},\ldots,q_{i3}$ and three square-slack
coordinates $\alpha_i,\beta_i,\gamma_i$. Abbreviate

$$
\begin{gathered}
r_i=t_ib_i,\qquad j_i=t_i+b_i(1-t_i^2),\qquad n_i=j_i+t_ib_i,\\
T_i=1+b_i,\quad U_i=1+2b_i,\quad
L_i=b_i^2+8b_i+4,\quad A_i=(8b_i-1)(5b_i+2).
\end{gathered}
\tag{1.7}
$$

Here $A_i$ is a source polynomial, not an action matrix. Define

$$
\begin{aligned}
q_{i4}&=-q_{i0}+4q_{i1}-6q_{i2}+4q_{i3},\\
q_{i5}&=-4q_{i0}+15q_{i1}-20q_{i2}+10q_{i3},\\
q_{i6}&=-10q_{i0}+36q_{i1}-45q_{i2}+20q_{i3},\\
q_{i7}&=-20q_{i0}+70q_{i1}-84q_{i2}+35q_{i3}.
\end{aligned}
\tag{1.8}
$$

Let $I_M$ be the rational polynomial ideal generated by the following
equations, for each label, together with the two inverse equations below:

$$
\begin{gathered}
q_{i0}+24+e_i=0,\qquad j_iq_{i1}+e_i=0,\\
5T_iq_{i2}-27+5e_i=0,\qquad n_iq_{i3}+e_i=0,\\
P_{\mathrm{raw},i}
=5e_i\{2L_ij_in_i-4T_iU_i(j_i+n_i)\}+6A_ij_in_i=0,\\
24+e_i+(U_i+n_i)q_{i5}-p=0,\\
24+e_i+(2U_i+n_i)q_{i6}-v=0,\\
24+e_i+(3U_i+2n_i)q_{i7}-m=0,\\
t_i\alpha_i^2-1=0,\qquad b_i\beta_i^2-1=0,\qquad
(1-t_ib_i)\gamma_i^2-1=0,
\end{gathered}
\tag{1.9}
$$

$$
\eta\bigl((t_1-t_2)^2+(b_1-b_2)^2\bigr)-1=0,
\qquad \pi(p-24)-1=0.
\tag{1.10}
$$

The variables $p,v,m$ are shared. All other variables belong to their
indicated label, except $\eta,\pi$. Treating $j_i,n_i,T_i,U_i$ as independent
coordinates and adjoining their defining equations gives the same incidence
after these uniquely defined coordinates are eliminated.

Put

$$
Q_M=T_1U_1j_1n_1T_2U_2j_2n_2,\qquad
J_M=I_M:Q_M^\infty,\qquad
\Delta_M=J_M\cap\mathbb Q[p,v].
\tag{1.11}
$$

For complex points define

$$
\mathcal Z_M=V_{\mathbb C}(I_M)\cap\{Q_M\ne0\},\qquad
\mathcal B_M=\overline{\operatorname{pr}_{p,v}(\mathcal Z_M)}^{\mathrm{Zar}}.
\tag{1.12}
$$

The complex inverse guard in (1.10) is retained literally. A nonzero
complex source difference can have zero squared sum; such a difference
does not satisfy this guard. Over the reals it is exactly source
distinctness.

